      "message": "Your current message doesn\u0027t explain this well. How about this instead?\n\n```suggestion\nDefer loading changes during ref visibility checks\n\nGit fetch and push for users without READ on refs/* perform full ref\nfiltering over many changes. For non-private entries,\nChangesByProjectCache stores branch and privacy metadata but no full\nChange. ChangeControl nevertheless loaded ChangeNotes in its constructor\nsolely to compute isNew and isOwner, adding storage I/O for every\nchange.\n\nDefer those computations until a permission requires them. The READ path\ncan now use cached non-private metadata and branch READ permission\nwithout loading the Change. Private entries continue using their\nexisting full Change and reviewer data.\n\nAdd a regression test that checks READ permission on non-private\nChangeData without a persisted Change.\n\nBug: Issue 462642961\nRelease-Notes: Fix slow git fetch/push for users lacking READ on refs/*\nChange-Id: Ia36fd096284bd71f5e13e4ed579d601d7a2af19d\n```",
